WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.304
Gate four is AWS Health, which
publishes issues, scheduled changes

2
00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:08.712
and account notifications per
account, with the affected resources.

3
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:10.775
It's the one provider with a cost.

4
00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:15.169
AWS's documentation says the account
needs a qualifying support plan,

5
00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:19.412
and without one the API answers
with a subscription-required error.

6
00:00:19.412 --> 00:00:22.801
AWS's own pages name the
qualifying plans differently,

7
00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:25.738
so check the account
against the current pages.

8
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:30.305
The reader holds a customer managed
policy with three describe actions,

9
00:00:30.305 --> 00:00:34.186
because AWS publishes no read-only
managed policy for Health,

10
00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:36.926
and its full-access
policy includes writes.

11
00:00:36.926 --> 00:00:39.285
Then cross-check from the Health endpoint,

12
00:00:39.285 --> 00:00:43.938
which is US East for commercial accounts
and the GovCloud West region for GovCloud.

13
00:00:43.938 --> 00:00:44.913
And collect.

14
00:00:44.913 --> 00:00:46.538
Until the reader exists,

15
00:00:46.538 --> 00:00:51.088
an EventBridge rule on AWS Health
events pushes scheduled changes.

16
00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:56.620
Without a support plan, the AWS Health
Dashboard and its email are the only path.
